; Elrond greets the player
;
; Script handler (op 3, in Elrond's script #R$C99A). When Elrond is where the
; player is (ActorLocation = PlayerLocation) he says "Hello". Otherwise it
; returns before the test pass accepts, so the script takes its alternative
; step (#R$C9A4).
; .
; Hardware: none (the text goes through the message printer).
@label=ElrondGreets
c$A525 LD A,($B6F6)  ; location of the NPC being run
 $A528 LD HL,$B6F5
 $A52B CP (HL)
 $A52C RET NZ        ; not with the player: refuse
 $A52D CALL $9D44
 $A530 LD HL,$B05F   ; "Hello"
 $A533 JP $A1E3
